Theorem RL-8: Shared requires mutation isolation

  Preconditions:
    - Uniqueness(v) = Shared proves multiple logical owners.
    - DP-5 forbids same-identity mutation for Shared.
    - DP-9's historical `StaticShared` label denotes IsolationRequired.

  Soundness property:
    Forall owned Shared value v at a mutation point:
      (P1) IsolationRequired regardless of borrow state.
      (P2) satisfying isolation preserves every existing owner's view.
    The theorem does not require copying; copying is one possible projection.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate no-borrow and active-borrow Shared cases.
    Coverage gate: 2 cases.

    Negative-direction witness:
      SameIdentityAdmissible for Shared is rejected because another owner would
      observe the mutation.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl8_static_shared_mutation)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-8 freezes mutation isolation for both Shared borrow states and rejects same-identity mutation without selecting a copy mechanism
